* subquery is nothing more than query inside another query
* we use it to select new column, 
                      to create a filter,
                      to create a consolidated source from which to select the data.

#subquery to create a new column

SELECT
  column 1,
  column2,
  (select 
        ..
      from table_2
      group by 1)
from table_1
group by 1;

##Practice_Q_1
If we want to see the number of playlists in the app to which the users added each song

SELECT name,
  (select count(playlist_id),
          from playlist_track
   where playlist_track.track_id= track.track_id) as no_of_playlists
from track 
group by 1
order  by no_of_playlists desc
limit 50;

##Practice_Q_2
We want to know the % of tracks of each genre in our database

SELECT genre,
     round(cast(count(track_id) as float) / count(*) from track),2) as per_of_song
 from genre
inner join track on
genre.genre_id = track.genre_id
group by 1
order by 2 desc;

